{
  "note": "Configured MCP headers carry a canary. Across three runs the canary was present on every request the client sent, including the request that returned 500. But an HTTP 500 did NOT trigger a retry: with the outage during the handshake the client stopped, and with it on tools/call the call failed and no further request followed. So 'headers re-sent on reconnect' could not be observed, and the sharper finding is that reconnect does not cover HTTP 500 outages.",
